-# ---- THE STANDING LEARNING LOOP (each solve compounds onto the next) ----
-# A new game's solver flow, all in the harness, zero quota:
-#   1. recommend_approach(game)  [arc_solve_learning] — route to the closest SOLVED
-#      game's proven recipe by survey-feature similarity (reverse-engineer only the delta).
-#   2. OfflineSolver(..., verifier=v)  [arc_solver_kit] — verifier-routed BEST-FIRST
-#      search; an energy/goal-distance score prunes the search. Demonstrated on lp85:
-#      3860 (plain BFS) -> 359 states = 10.75x fewer (arc3_verifier_routed_search_demo).
-#   3. LearnedVerifier  [arc_value_learner] — train the verifier on our OWN solve
-#      traces (state->steps-to-go); it improves from each solve. Demonstrated on lp85:
-#      trained on L1-L2, cut HELD-OUT L3 search 3163 -> 338 states = 9.36x fewer,
-#      approaching the hand-tuned bound (286) without being told the heuristic
-#      (arc3_learned_verifier_demo).
-#   4. reproduce(...)  [arc_solver_kit] — the offline reproduction GATE; only
-#      reproduced levels count.
-#   5. update this registry (win-condition, action-model, gotchas, DEAD-ENDS).
-# Learns from SUCCESSES (recipe routing + trained verifier) and FAILURES (dead-ends).
-# Next: train the verifier CROSS-game (transfer the value head), and A* (path-cost +
-# learned heuristic) for leaderboard action-efficiency, not just search compute.
