-  # The search (graph_explore_solve_v2) takes an optional A*-style goal heuristic. We have two,
-  # and they are NOT interchangeable -- the selector picks by measured per-action CELL IMPACT
-  # (median cells one action changes, from a few banked transitions):
-  #   - cell_count_distance (Hamming): best for LOW cell-impact games (su15 ~20 cells/action;
-  #     cell-count ~= move-count). Over-estimates move-distance on high-impact games -> greedy.
-  #   - misplaced_region_distance (8-conn wrong-region count): best for HIGH cell-impact games
-  #     (r11l~70 / sk48~74 / m0r0~100). Move-aligned (one action ~ fixes one region) -> finds the
-  #     OPTIMAL path with far fewer expansions (r11l 3-act @257 vs BFS 2236; sk48 -43%; m0r0
-  #     solves where BFS exhausts 8000). NEVER regressed across the 8-game validation.
-  #   - bfs (no heuristic): the complete fallback, and the CORRECT choice when NO win-state/target
-  #     is known yet (a first-ever solve) -- a goal-distance heuristic needs a target.
-  # RULE (arc_heuristic_select.recommend_order): no target -> bfs; cell-impact >= ~40 ->
-  #   region_count first; < 40 -> cell_count first; bfs always last.
-  # DYNAMIC ADAPTATION to unseen games: select_best() runs the portfolio, reproduction-gates each,
-  #   picks the winner (path-optimality then expansions), and BANKS it to gap_fills/. The standing
-  #   loop (arc_loop_solve.solve_via_explore) calls bank_for_solved_game() after every fresh solve,
-  #   so each new game's best heuristic is learned + captured live (guarded, never breaks the solve).
-  #   recommend_approach() now surfaces this policy in every new-game recipe.
-  # CAPTURED (reproduction-gated gap_fills/): su15=cell_count; r11l/ls20/m0r0/sk48=region_count.
-  # TO EXTEND (add a new heuristic): register it in arc_heuristic_select.factory()/HEURISTIC_NAMES
-  #   + add its selection condition to recommend_order; it then joins the portfolio automatically.
-  # ADAPTER-FREE FALLBACK (first contact, no per-game RE): scripts/arc_loop_solve.py
-  # routes an un-adaptered game to graph_explore_solve (arc_graph_explore.py); if it
-  # advances a level it CAPTURES the trajectory -> reproduction-gates it -> trains a
-  # verifier-seed (generic grid features) -> persists the trajectory as the adapter
-  # seed, so the NEXT solve is the efficient verifier-routed loop, not blind explore.
-  # graph_explore_solve_v2 = SYSTEMATIC frontier BFS over the state-transition graph
-  # (shortest-path-to-untested-state-action, replay-navigation) -- toward arXiv:2512.24156.
-  # SOLVES ADAPTER-FREE (full capture->gate->seed pipeline, NO per-game RE):
-  #   ls20 L1 (v2, 13 actions); r11l L1 (v2 + rich_action_candidates, 3 actions -- shorter
-  #   than the recorded 4). Both offline_reproduced=True via the standing loop.
-  #   2026-06-17 SWEEP (scripts/arc_explore_sweep.py over all 19 unsolved games) added
-  #   FOUR more, all re-gated reproduced=True L1: cd82 (5 kbd), sp80 (4 kbd), su15 (7
-  #   diagonal clicks), tu93 (18 kbd nav). 14/19 resisted at L0 (deeper win-mechanics);
-  #   tn36 ERRORED (its ACTION6 wants a non-{x,y} click payload -> per-game delta-RE).
-  #   Net: the systematic explorer cracks the SHALLOW-win tail for free; the residual is
-  #   the genuinely-deep games + per-game click-schema deltas.
-  # rich_action_candidates fixed r11l: every detected object is a click candidate (its
-  #   winning clicks were objects #15/#27 dropped by the old 12-cap).
-  # graph_explore_solve_v3 = value/novelty-guided best-first (optional verifier=predicted
-  #   steps-to-go -> the learned verifier feeds back; else count-based novelty + depth bias;
-  #   frame-change-only transitions). For the DEEP/HARD tail.
-  # HARD TAIL (still no-advance generically): wa30 L1 ~33-deep keyboard navigation.
-  #   CROSS-GAME VALUE TRANSFER built (scripts/arc_cross_game_verifier_train.py:
-  #   pool r11l+ls20+lp85 trajectories -> game-agnostic frame features -> normalized
-  #   steps-to-go -> a transferred verifier wired into v3). HONEST A/B on wa30: cross-game
-  #   verifier does NOT help (both no-advance; 66s vs 77s). Generic grid features
-  #   (nonzero/colors/objects/spread/dominant) don't transfer to wa30's game-specific
-  #   progress signal -- mirrors the project's domain-bound-verifier finding. CONCLUSION:
-  #   the deep/sparse hard tail needs PER-GAME RE (an adapter) or a much richer LEARNED
-  #   representation (more solved games + a learned frame encoder), NOT generic transfer.
-  # CALIBRATED ARC STRATEGY: easy/medium -> adapter-free systematic explore (r11l,ls20 work);
-  #   adaptered -> verifier-routed efficient solve (lp85, self-improving); hard/deep -> per-game RE.
-  # BUDGET FINDING (2026-06-17 ablation, operator "if the larger budget is not helping
-  # roll it back"). The effort budget is a PER-TASK-TYPE decision, not a global knob:
-  #   - DISCOVERY sweep (first-level on a NEW game): ~12000 expansions is load-bearing.
-  #     cn04/m0r0/sk48 were each re-confirmed to NO-ADVANCE at the 4000 default (even
-  #     with E1 salience+mask) and only solve at >4000. The 4000->12000 bump earned +3
-  #     games. Use ~12000 for a thorough discovery sweep.
-  #   - +1-LEVEL ADVANCE (next level on a SOLVED game): budget does NOT help. Raising it
-  #     to 30000 produced 0 reproducible advances (ls20 burned 1218s; sp80 "found" L2 but
-  #     reproduced=False — hidden state beyond HUD-masking). This frontier is
